{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Hushim</b> — twice in the Masorah, from two linguistic forms: <b>וּבְנֵי דָן חֻשִׁים</b> and <b>וְאַנְחְנוּ נֶחְלְצָה חֻשִׁים</b>. We say in the chapter Mi SheMet that the sons of Dan were like reeds of cane — meaning below it is one, and above it splits into several stalks; from one son he had, many emerged. So too <b>נחלץ חשים</b> — for the way of those who do battle is to cleave to one another, that the enemies not separate them."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:18:30.477710368Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}